                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "There are six equally likely positions for the single head.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The single head can occur in any of six positions. Each sequence has probability $\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{exactly one head})&=6\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^6\\\\P(\\text{exactly one head})&=\\frac{6}{64}\\\\P(\\text{exactly one head})&=\\frac{3}{32}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
