                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Subtract the probabilities of zero heads and exactly one head from 1.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The complementary cases are zero heads and exactly one head. They are mutually exclusive.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at least two heads})&=1-P(\\text{zero heads})-P(\\text{exactly one head})\\\\P(\\text{at least two heads})&=1-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^6-6\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^6\\\\P(\\text{at least two heads})&=1-\\frac{1}{64}-\\frac{6}{64}\\\\P(\\text{at least two heads})&=\\frac{57}{64}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
